  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A project to improve Health conditions for the IDPs and cyclone affected people in Sittwe,Rakhine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspangtThis one-year project will provide health services including mainstreaming of explosive ordnance
risk education and mental health and psychosocial support not only for the
Internally Displaced People and vulnerable people but also cyclone mocha
affected people located in Sittwe Township, Rakhine State. For the health
component, MERCY Malaysia will provide comprehensive health care services in
Sittwe township through two mobile clinic teams. The comprehensive primary
health care services include reproductive healthcare, maternal and childcare,
non-communicable diseases, and preventing, detecting, and rapidly responding to
any communicable disease outbreak. Mental health and psychosocial support services will also be provided to the beneficiaries. In line with the protection sector, explosive
ordnance risk education is to be provided to the IDPs, and vulnerable people in
Sittwe township since MERCY Malaysia&#x2019;s staffs had already been trained by Mine
Advisory Group during the previous MHF- 23142 project. Cyclone affected health
facilities and clinics will also be repaired. The project is designed to ensure
not only for the Internally Displaced People and vulnerable people but also for
cyclone mocha affected people located in Sittwe Township have continuous access
to essential health&#xA0;care including explosive ordnance risk education
and MHPSS services. lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
